{
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Provenance notes for entries that were deliberately dropped or moved
  // (recoverable from git history):
  //
  // Pathfinder - REMOVED: an objective description was mis-attributed to a
  // nonexistent quest ("Sales Night"); it rewrote a correct type=visit
  // objective ("Visit the Railway Exfil exit on Interchange", confirmed by both
  // captures + tarkov.dev) into fabricated text.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Pathfinder
  //
  // Power of Persuasion (aka "Test Drive - Part 2") - MOVED to
  // src/overrides/modes/regular/tasks.json5: a mode divergence - wiki
  // (regular) = 20 PMCs on Streets/GZ/Interchange; 1.1-pve data = 5 on
  // Woods/GZ/Interchange/Customs.
  //
  // Easy-Breezy (aka "Test Drive - Part 5") - MOVED to
  // src/overrides/modes/regular/tasks.json5: a mode divergence - wiki
  // (regular) = 50 targets on Factory; 1.1-pve data = 30 on
  // Reserve/Lighthouse.
  //
  // Small Business - Part 3 - REMOVED: the two Woods objective descriptions
  // were swapped, contradicting tarkov.dev, BOTH game captures, and the wiki
  // guide. Re-add only with a fresh in-game marker screenshot.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Small_Business_-_Part_3
  //
  // Setup - REMOVED: the API serves the same 9 hat/vest combinations
  // (verified: normalized item-id sets are identical; only ordering differed).
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Setup
  //
  // Establish Contact, Collector, Is This a Reference? - REMOVED (issue #274):
  // these were authored as "Fence LL1" but are actually Fence *reputation*
  // (scav karma) gates. json.tarkov.dev now serves the correct discriminated
  // requirement (reputation >= 4 / >= 3 / >= 1) and the wiki agrees, so the
  // ambiguous LL1 entry would both mislabel the semantic and - under
  // replace-array semantics - strip the upstream requirement. Proof:
  //   https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Establish_Contact (scav karma +4)
  //   https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Collector (scav karma +3 + 7x LL4)
  //   https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Is_This_a_Reference%3F (scav karma +1)
  //
  // minPlayerLevel overrides (A Fuel Matter, Inventory Check, Psycho Sniper,
  // Bullshit, Chumming, ...) - REMOVED: the 1.1-pve data carries no Level
  // conditions for these quests.
  //
  // The original Season 1 LL1-LL4 batch was removed after its requirement
  // claims proved unreliable. The active traderRequirements later in this file
  // are a separately re-audited set: entries already supplied upstream were
  // retired, while the remaining corrections are verified against the current
  // reference/API comparison and kept only where still load-bearing.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  // District Patrol - quest XP reworked in 1.1.0.0
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/District_Patrol
  // Verified: the 1.1-pve data; wiki agrees.
  //
  // The 1.1.0.0 patch consolidated quest XP to a small set of standard
  // values; tarkov.dev still serves stale pre-1.1 values for the tasks marked
  // "quest XP reworked in 1.1.0.0" in this file, in every mode. Both the wiki
  // and the 1.1-pve data agree on the corrected
  // values, and each entry is recorded in src/divergences/tasks.json5
  // (status: converged).
  '64e7b9bffd30422ed03dad38': {
    traderRequirements: [
      {
        id: 'overlay.64e7b9bffd30422ed03dad38.54cb50c76803fa8b248b4571.level.>=.2',
        requirementType: 'level',
        compareMethod: '>=',
        trader: { id: '54cb50c76803fa8b248b4571', name: 'Prapor' },
        value: 2,
      }, // Was: [] (player level requirement, minPlayerLevel 20)
    ],
    experience: 10000, // Was: 8300 (all modes, stale pre-1.1 value)
  },

  // Glory to CPSU (old: Glory to CPSU - Part 1) - Renamed
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Glory_to_CPSU
  // The old "Glory to CPSU - Part 1" page is historical; the S1 quest is a
  // single "Glory to CPSU" (dropped "- Part 1") with reworked optional
  // objectives.
  '639135b04ed9512be67647d7': {
    name: 'Glory to CPSU', // Was: Glory to CPSU - Part 1
  },

  // Escort - quest XP reworked in 1.1.0.0
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Escort
  // Verified: the 1.1-pve data; wiki agrees.
  '60e71b62a0beca400d69efc4': {
    traderRequirements: [
      {
        id: 'overlay.60e71b62a0beca400d69efc4.54cb50c76803fa8b248b4571.level.>=.4',
        requirementType: 'level',
        compareMethod: '>=',
        trader: { id: '54cb50c76803fa8b248b4571', name: 'Prapor' },
        value: 4,
      }, // Was: [] (player level requirement, minPlayerLevel 46)
    ],
    experience: 65000, // Was: 155000 (all modes, stale pre-1.1 value)
    objectives: {
      // The wiki lists eight objectives, one per map, each for 2 PMCs. The API
      // serves nine: this one duplicates 65e19abadf39d26751b3bb1e, which
      // already covers Ground Zero and Ground Zero 21+ with a count of 2.
      //
      // It is not game data. tarkov-data-manager adds it by hand in
      // data/changed_quests.json under objectivesAdded - one of only four in
      // that file - alongside the same stale pre-1.1 experience value
      // corrected above. Removing it there is the real fix; until then this
      // keeps it out of the completion count instead of asking for four kills
      // the quest never wanted.
      //
      // Marked optional rather than given count 2: the objective should not
      // exist at all, and a plausible count would make it indistinguishable
      // from the eight real ones.
      // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Escort
      '65e09b343458a36a766837c7': {
        optional: true, // Was: false
      },
    },
  },

